                <Title>Bati-MultiDialectalASR-Dataset</Title>
                <Description>This dataset contains paired audio and text resources for three Bati dialects (Kelleng, Mbougue, and Nyambat), which belong to the Yambasa group of Bantu languages found in Cameroon. It contains 13,344 audio clips totalling 6 hours, 8 minutes and 12.286 seconds and 44 audio/text mapping files totalling 13,346 lines. Due to its cross-dialectal nature, the dataset is suitable for multilingual automatic speech recognition tasks.</Description>
